Description: Computes and estimates stress-strength reliability R = P(Y < X)
    for any pair of continuous distributions given by their density and
    distribution functions, including standard R families found by name.
    Beyond the single-component model it covers multi-stress environments,
    the three-variable model P(Z < Y < X), s-out-of-k systems and cascade
    systems. Parameters are estimated by maximum likelihood, maximum product
    of spacings, least squares, weighted least squares, Cramer-von Mises and
    Anderson-Darling methods, by jackknife and bootstrap bias correction, and
    by Bayesian Metropolis-Hastings sampling. Confidence intervals for R are
    given by the delta method, the parametric bootstrap and posterior
    intervals, and a Monte Carlo engine reports bias, mean squared error and
    coverage over grids of sample sizes and parameters.
